# The rules no fixture under tests/reject states, one line each: the rule's
# phrase, a tab, its kind, a tab, why. tests/spec/rules-covered reads this
# file: every rule the build's list (IdrRules.txt) names has a fixture whose
# `-- expect:` header names it, or a line here, never both. `unreachable`:
# no source program reaches the refusal. `elsewhere`: another pool reaches
# it. `owed`: a source program reaches it; its fixture is written when a
# build shows one.
io primitive	unreachable	no site raises it: no reject in compiler/src names it and no Rule::IOPrimitive is in foreign/idr; registry entries name it only in their rules lists (Registry/Primitives.idr:75, 92, 158, 175, 341, 348)
identity hook	unreachable	no site raises it: registry entries name it only in their rules lists (Registry/Recognized.idr:32, 126, 162, 200)
compiled module	unreachable	raised when the compiled module the frontend reads lacks a definition or a constructor it names (Translate/Closed.idr:1118, Translate/Keys.idr:791, Translate/Types.idr:663, Translate/Cases.idr:734, 769), which no module Idris checked lacks
runtime	unreachable	raised by the driver when the runtime object it links lacks a member (foreign/idr/lib/Driver/ReadRuntime.cpp:166): the toolchain's object, not a program
library	unreachable	never alone: user code reaches an untrusted package's definition only through an import of its module, refused as program at the import (Frontend/Program.idr:174-178); the definitions PrimIO does not admit are types no value of user code has (GCPtr, GCAnyPtr, ThreadID)
data type	unreachable	raised for a data type whose constructors Idris does not record, an [external] type (Translate/Types.idr:635); a value of one that is no runtime handle comes only from %foreign, refused as escape hatch first (Frontend/Profile.idr:330)
definition	unreachable	raised for a reached definition that is not pattern matching (Translate/Programs.idr:54); Idris elaborates every definition of a source as one, and the reach check refuses or hooks the others, primitives, %extern, %foreign and holes, before translation (Frontend/Profile.idr:312-330)
string primitive	unreachable	raised for a literal match on a constant that is no literal, a primitive type or the world (Translate/Cases.idr:809); a match on a type value is a type in a runtime position, refused as type, and user code has no world to match
hook	elsewhere	raised when a registry entry does not match the library definition it names (Frontend/Profile.idr:329, Frontend/Program.idr:99, Translate/Terms.idr:419, 856, 860, Translate/Cases.idr:511); a program reaches it by shadowing a library module, as tests/registry/base-surface and tests/registry/broken-entry do
static argument	owed	raised for a type parameter, shape or implementation no compile-time analysis fixes, or one partially applied (Translate/Instances.idr:164, 179, 191, Translate/Terms.idr:705, Translate/Cases.idr:676)
match	owed	raised for a match on an erased value between several alternatives (Translate/Cases.idr:580); the literal match without a default (:485) cannot occur, as Idris never finds a match on literals complete
